The {{i_open_the_activity_chooser}} step fails on Chrome because it tries to track the first “Add content” on the page, which is hidden.

This is currently in the skip tag injector: [https://github.com/moodlehq/moodle-skip-tag-injector/commit/4a4b39a58a6a20cfc3ad5f913c2232fca88e4982|https://github.com/moodlehq/moodle-skip-tag-injector/commit/4a4b39a58a6a20cfc3ad5f913c2232fca88e4982|smart-link] 

Something like this shoudl address the issue:

{noformat}diff --git a/public/course/tests/behat/behat_course.php b/public/course/tests/behat/behat_course.php
index 8e3a66cbd2..5ac268a466 100644
--- a/public/course/tests/behat/behat_course.php
+++ b/public/course/tests/behat/behat_course.php
@@ -2183,10 +2183,14 @@ class behat_course extends behat_base {
      */
     public function i_open_the_activity_chooser() {
         // Open the "Activity or resource and Subsection" dropdown first.
-        $this->execute('behat_general::i_click_on',
-                ['//button[@data-action="open-addingcontent"]', 'xpath_element']);
-        $this->execute('behat_general::i_click_on',
-            ['//button[@data-action="open-chooser"]', 'xpath_element']);
+        $this->execute('behat_general::i_click_on', [
+            '.always-visible button[data-action="open-addingcontent"]',
+            'css_element',
+        ]);
+        $this->execute('behat_general::i_click_on', [
+            '.always-visible button[data-action="open-chooser"]',
+            'css_element',
+        ]);

         $node = $this->get_selected_node('xpath_element', '//div[@data-region="modules"]');
         $this->ensure_node_is_visible($node);{noformat}

In [https://moodle.atlassian.net/browse/MDL-89290|https://moodle.atlassian.net/browse/MDL-89290|smart-link], support for admin notification CTAs was implemented via {{core_admin/notification_ctas.mustache}}. In this template, feature highlights/ticks are hardcoded directly in the loop:

{code:html}{{#ticks}}
    <li><i class="icon fa fa-check-circle admin-notification-cta-tick" aria-hidden="true"></i> {{text}}</li>
{{/ticks}}
{code}

Because {{{{text}}}} uses standard Mustache HTML escaping, passing raw HTML (such as {{<a>}} anchor tags) renders as plain text. Additionally, because the tick list item logic is tightly coupled within the primary {{notification_ctas}} template, third-party themes cannot customise how ticks are structured without overriding the entire template.

h4. *Expected behaviour*

The template should support links within the tick items natively, and/or extract the tick rendering into a dedicated sub-template/partial so that third-party themes can easily override tick rendering behaviour without taking on the maintenance burden of replacing the full {{notification_ctas}} template.
